    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": false,
    "title": "interfaces: fix findAncestorByHash false positive",
    "user": {
      "login": "Romansage6",
      "id": 182553131,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOCuGKKw",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/182553131?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Romansage6",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Romansage6",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Romansage6/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Romansage6/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Romansage6/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Romansage6/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Romansage6/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Romansage6/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Romansage6/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Romansage6/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Romansage6/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "findAncestorByHash looks up both block_hash and ancestor_hash, then was\nonly supposed to clear the ancestor pointer when the lookups succeeded\nbut the ancestor relationship didn't hold:\n\n```cpp\nif (block && ancestor && block->GetAncestor(ancestor->nHeight) != ancestor) ancestor = nullptr;\n```\n\nBecause of the `&&` short circuit, an unknown `block_hash` makes the\nwhole condition false without ever evaluating the relationship check,\nso a successful `ancestor_hash` lookup is passed through unmodified\nand the function reports `true` for a descendant that doesn't exist.\n\nBefore:\n```cpp\nchain->findAncestorByHash(uint256{}, active[0]->GetBlockHash()) // returns true\n```\n\nAfter this change it correctly returns `false` when either hash is\nunknown, in addition to the existing relationship check.\n\nTested with:\n```\ncmake --build build --target test_bitcoin -j8\n./build/bin/test_bitcoin --run_test=interfaces_tests\n```\nFull suite (`./build/bin/test_bitcoin`, 877 cases) also passes with no\nregressions. Added two new cases to `interfaces_tests/findAncestorByHash`\ncovering unknown `block_hash` and unknown `ancestor_hash`, which fail\non master and pass with this fix.\n\nFixes #36472",
