      ],
      "message": "interfaces: fix findAncestorByHash false positive\n\nfindAncestorByHash looked up both block_hash and ancestor_hash, then\ncleared the ancestor pointer only when both lookups succeeded but the\nancestor relationship did not hold:\n\n  if (block && ancestor && block->GetAncestor(...) != ancestor)\n      ancestor = nullptr;\n\nBecause of the && short circuit, an unknown block_hash made the whole\ncondition false without ever running the relationship check, so a\nsuccessful ancestor_hash lookup was passed through unmodified and the\nfunction reported true for a descendant that does not exist.\n\nClear the ancestor whenever either lookup fails, not only when the\nrelationship check fails.\n\nAdd unit test cases for an unknown block_hash and an unknown\nancestor_hash, matching the reported regression.\n\nFixes #36472",
